## Migration method (for the record)

Debug/interpolation call sites in tests/semantics/semantics.mbt and
tests/robust/robust.mbt interpolated `String?` / `Int?` values directly,
routing through the deprecated core `Show for X?` impl (warning [0020])
and `StringBuilder::new` (deprecated constructor). Migration:
  - robust.mbt: `StringBuilder::new()` -> `StringBuilder()`; new local
    helper `opt_str(String?) -> String` renders `None` / `Some(v)`.
  - semantics.mbt: same `opt_str` plus `opt_int(Int?) -> String` for the
    T-09 `rule_index` fields.
  Every `\{x.field}` Option interpolation became `\{opt_str(x.field)}`
  / `\{opt_int(x.field)}`. The rendered strings are byte-identical to
  the previous Show output, so all uap-core golden assertions are
  unchanged (verified: suite green on native and js — see counts in this
  file's sibling evidence and the task report). Struct-level
  interpolations (`\{info.browser}` etc.) keep using the retained
  derive(Show) and never produced [0020] warnings.
  The core-debug-README alternative (`\{Repr(value)} via a
  moonbitlang/core/debug import) was rejected because (a) it changes the
  rendered goldens (Debug quotes strings inside Some) and (b) it would
  require editing moon.pkg files, which are outside this task's
  ownership boundary.

